  "verdict": "CONCERNS",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "`AssignmentSource.queued` is evaluated once at import, so every instance records the same stale timestamp",
      "description": "`queued: datetime = timezone.now()` runs when the class body executes, not per instance. Every `AssignmentSource` built without an explicit `queued` gets the same import-time value. `to_dict()` copies it (lines 27-28), and `sync_group_assignee_outbound` ships it to the task as `assignment_source_dict` (`src/sentry/integrations/utils/sync.py:141-143`). Any assignment made after the process started therefore carries the wrong queue time. Nothing in `src/sentry/integrations` reads `queued`, so there is no current behavior impact. The fix is `field(default_factory=timezone.now)`.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py:18"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "`from_dict` returns None on a TypeError without logging, so a malformed source silently bypasses the same-integration loop guard",
      "description": "`from_dict` catches `(ValueError, TypeError)` and returns `None` with no log. A dict whose keys don't match the dataclass fields makes `cls(**input_dict)` raise `TypeError`. `ValueError` can't be raised here, since the dataclass doesn't validate. The caller at `src/sentry/integrations/tasks/sync_assignee_outbound.py:53-56` then passes `None` to `should_sync`. That skips the guard at `src/sentry/integrations/mixins/issues.py:390-391`, so the assignment is sent back to the integration that originated it, which is the sync cycle the guard exists to prevent. The normal `to_dict()` \u2192 `from_dict()` path round-trips cleanly. This only fires on schema drift or a hand-built payload, and nothing is logged when it does.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "error-handling-observability",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py:30-35"
    }
  ],
